omx-clap-host (0.21.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging checks: list fault-14.clap and jack_identity, wrap the tests
    description
  * omx-clap-host-tests: ship fault-14.clap and jack_identity, the culprit
    and the feeder of a chain test (#104)
  * 0.21.0: the release dated, the fuzz harnesses' own limits named (#345)
  * README: version 0.21.0
  * abi: the baseline recorded at 0.21.0, omx_clap_chain_order and
    omx_clap_host_name_slot added (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: open_jack_client's name out is given, not opened (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: a termination signal on any thread finishes the socket
    once (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: a client's name copied at its open, never read back (#104)
  * doc, changelog: the role named in a slot, the first cycle wet (#104)
  * tests: the parity fixture ten times at 96 kHz, pass on the role (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: a client's first cycle runs the plugin, never dry (#104)
  * core: a carrier's thread on the audio role from its slot, no lock (#104)
  * tests, doc: chain_end's lock among the sites no stress turns red (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: the new lines wrapped at 120 columns (#104)
  * doc, changelog: the role lock as it is held, the core's role race named
    (#104)
  * tests: a hold shows JACK's thread never waits on the role lock (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: JACK's thread never waits on the audio role's lock (#104)
  * tests: drills for a stopped member's links after the rollback (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: a stopped member runs again with its links (#104)
  * doc, changelog: a line that removes and moves, another head all or none,
    one role lock (#104)
  * tests: the audio role's race unsuppressed, drills for another head, the
    core in the RT scan (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: another head all or none, a refused order answered (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: an instance's audio role under one lock, g_chain_members
    (#104)
  * fuzz_manifest: the rule's limit of 16 declarations is the harness's own
    (#345)
  * fuzz_preset: the grammar's depth of 32 is the harness's own (#345)
  * fuzz_preset: a compact write with a failed allocation gives no text (#345)
  * fuzz_preset: the rewritten member holds the value the rewrite set (#345)
  * chain.md: state the order-bank flip, name no private issue (#104)
  * ci, changelog: the host's chain under ThreadSanitizer, the library's
    order (#104)
  * tests: the hostd chain drill asserts every recorder heard the source
    (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: a chain's move in one walk, aux members refused, a line's
    clients made first (#104)
  * doc: a chain line's move is one walk, its refusals and JACK failures
    change nothing (#104)
  * core: omx_clap_chain_order publishes a chain's new order as one walk
    (#104)
  * doc: omx_clap_chain_order, a chain's members in a new order in one walk
    (#104)
  * 0.21.0: omx-clap-host runs plugin-hostd's chain line in one JACK client
    (#104)
  * doc: what a chain member costs on r1 (#104)
  * bench: chain-cost.sh, what a chain member costs against a client of its
    own (#104)
  * omx-clap-host: the chain's members walked under a lock off the cycle
    (#104)
  * ci: run the chain line's tests, its crash drill and its sabotage (#104)
  * tests: make test-chain-host-sabotage, each guard of the host's chain red
    (#104)
  * tests: make test-hostd-chain, a chain's crash drill behind plugin-hostd
    (#104)
  * tests: make test-chain-host, the chain line in one client end to end
    (#104)
  * chain identity and the bench declare the chain by the line (#104)
  * omx-clap-host runs plugin-hostd's chain line in one JACK client (#104)
  * doc: omx-clap-host runs plugin-hostd's chain line in one JACK client
    (#104)

